 "says": "Ana founds a Team on her laptop from an exact self-founded proposal that names the initial rules by digest; the owner commits the Team's policy, Ana's grant, its active state and profile, and moves the Team head. No provider is configured anywhere. Ana issues a QR invitation under that policy. On a second device, Ben binds his own device key, keeps the Team authority's out-of-band verification of that exact key, and consents to the exact invitation naming the invitation, his key binding and the verification. Ana then commits the membership change that names the invitation and Ben's consent, and Ben's membership comes back active. Every Team change expects the head the previous one moved to. What must come back: an active membership for Ben whose standing names both the invitation and the consent; what must not happen: any step needing a provider sign-in or an external identity.",
 "spec_sha256": "faa309cf0cf9a1bf58bab76908b8722e2a4cc711d7133ac35cf85803d6e86fd9",
 "steps": [
  {
   "carries": [
    "team_proposal",
    "team_rules"
   ],
   "head": "team_head_1",
   "name": "found_team",
   "process": "laptop",
   "request": "found_team",
   "result": "found_team_result",
   "returns": [
